 "meta": {
  "title": "Outreach email",
  "description": "An email, 600 wide (never a post): the Email frame is the email's card and each child is a section, top to bottom. Restyle it in the brand with set_tokens (color.brand for the button and pill, color.ink, color.paper the card, color.page around it, color.night the footer; font.heading, font.body), put the business's name in Logo and FooterName (or replace Logo with the logo as an image layer named for its alt text) and its own words everywhere. {{field}} words are filled for each person; keep them. A layer named link:<address> links: rename it to the real address. Save it as a template with email_design_save, declaring its fields. Outreach, one email a person (marketing with no topic, sent with email_batch): Body is each draft's own words, so keep {{body}} as it is and design around it: the header, an optional headline, the sign-off with the sender's name and role, one button if the outreach asks for a call. Fields: subject and body. Subject \"{{subject}}\". Marketing: keep Unsubscribe and {{address}} in the footer."
 },
